@startuml pipeline_stages
!include palette.iuml
title How does a change go from idea to merge?

|Agent|
start
if (new repository?) then (yes)
  :project-setup;
  note right
    AGENTS.md, decision log and
    agent workflows (committed)
  end note
endif
:decide: ask each open choice;
note right : the decision log (committed)
|Maintainer|
:choose;
|Agent|
:spec: write and verify;
note right : .private/specs/<slug>
:fresh session: implement
maps the code and plans;
|Maintainer|
:approve the plan
and the isolation;
|Agent|
:isolated-work, when approved:
worktree and branch;
note right
  ../<repository>-<slug>,
  branch <type>/<slug>
end note
repeat
  :one step: test first,
  commit, log;
  note right : .private/progress/<slug>
repeat while (more steps?) is (yes)
repeat
  :gates (gate-runner)
  and review (reviewer);
  note right : results and their commit in the progress log
  if (the changed approach failed,\na blocker or major finding\non the second review pass,\nor a SKIP or INCOMPLETE gate\nthe code cannot fix?) then (yes)
    :stop and report
    to the maintainer;
    note right : the evidence in the progress log and the handoff
    end
  endif
repeat while (FAIL, INCOMPLETE, SKIP\nor a blocker?) is (fix)
:session-close;
note right : .private/handoff/<date>-<slug>
|Maintainer|
:review the branch and
the pending decisions;
:go;
|Agent|
:land: rebase, gate the pinned
commit, fast-forward;
:remove the worktree and the branch;
|Maintainer|
:push;
stop

legend right
  Agent lane: skills and their subagents
  Maintainer lane: the maintainer's steps
  Notes: what a stage leaves, and where
endlegend
@enduml
